<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech CNB-120 index rises 0.5 points to 913.5.</title>
<headline>Czech CNB-120 index rises 0.5 points to 913.5.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The CNB-120 index, a broad daily measure of Czech equities, rose 0.5 points on Tuesday to 913.5, the Czech National Bank (CNB) said.</p>
<p>Eight of the ten sectoral indices fell, with the food index falling the most, down 26 points to 1,245.4.</p>
<p>Two indices rose, with the machinery index rising the most, up 9.8 points to 1227.1.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
